# Collider materials (project rule, Yury 18.09)

EVERY object in the game that carries a collider MUST get an explicit
PhysicsMaterial2D with a chosen friction and bounciness 0. Never rely on the
engine default: Unity's default is 0.4 and Box2D combines a pair as
sqrt(mu1 * mu2), so an unset material silently loses grip against a 1.2 surface.

- Ground: GroundBuilder builds `GroundDirt` from `groundFriction` (0.4).
- Human: Human.cs SoleMaterial (footFriction 1.2) and PalmMaterial (handFriction).
- Dog: has NOTHING today. `Dog.AddFriction` adds a `JointFriction` component, i.e.
  JOINT (angular) friction in the hinge - not contact. Give the chest, pelvis, head,
  tail and every paw an explicit material; the paw matches the human sole, the body
  lower. `pawFriction` under "Joint friction K" has nothing to do with grip.
- Anything added later (bird, tree, flower, campfire, platforms) needs the same.
- Values are chosen per part on purpose and live in code, never left implicit.
- Audit: for every `*Collider2D` in Assets check that `sharedMaterial` is assigned.
  A collider without a material is a bug.
